title: Day_6_End
---
// after hours, whoever you've been siding with comes looking for you
<<if $corporate > $workers>>
Your phone buzzes after closing. It's Corporate. She never calls this late.
Jennifer: You're still up. Good. I was going over your numbers.
Jennifer: They're not terrible. That's the nicest thing I've said to anyone this quarter.
-> Was that a compliment?
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: It was a performance review. Don't frame it.
    Jennifer: ...Fine. Frame it. Somewhere I can't see it.
-> Are you still at the office?
    Jennifer: Where else would I be? ...Don't answer that.
-> You could've just emailed.
    Jennifer: I could have. #scolding
Jennifer: Go to bed. I need you sharp tomorrow. For the *numbers*.
<<elseif $workers > $corporate>>
The girls have all gone home. Red Velvet is still sitting on the stall counter, watching the dunes go pink.
Red Velvet: Oh! Boss. I was just...erm...checking the stall. It's very checked. #cringe
Red Velvet: You know, nobody from corporate ever came out here after five. You're different.
-> Mind if I sit?
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: Oh! Erm...no! I mean yes. I mean sit! There's room. There's lots of room. #cringe
    You watch the sun go down. Neither of you mentions how much room there is.
-> Don't stay out too late.
    Red Velvet: I won't! Goodnight, boss.
<<endif>>
===
title: Day_11_End
---
<<if $corporate > $workers>>
Your phone rings. You pick up before the first ring is over, which she notices.
Jennifer: Eager. Good. The board saw your wage report. Flat as a desert, they loved it.
Jennifer: I told them I picked you myself.
Jennifer: I didn't, by the way. You were just the only one who didn't cry at the donuts.
-> So you did pick me.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: Don't push it.
    Jennifer: ...Yes.
-> Just doing my job.
    Jennifer: Then keep doing it. I'm getting used to these calls. I mean the *numbers*. #scolding
<<elseif $workers > $corporate>>
There's a knock on the shack door. Red Velvet is holding a cake box like it might explode.
Red Velvet: I made this. For the stall. But it came out wrong, so...erm...it's yours now.
Red Velvet: It's heart shaped. That's the wrong part. It was supposed to be round. I don't know what happened. #cringe
-> I love it.
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: You...okay! Good! That's good! I'm going to go now! Goodnight! #cringe
    She's gone before you can say goodnight back. The cake is very good.
-> Thanks, Red Velvet.
    Red Velvet: Anytime, boss! Don't let Honey see it, she'll want one.
<<endif>>
===
title: Day_14_End
---
<<if $corporate > $workers>>
Your phone rings. It's late. It's always late now.
Jennifer: Tomorrow's the big day. I wanted to make sure you hadn't wandered into a dune.
Jennifer: If you hit the number, they'll bring you to headquarters. There's an empty office on the top floor.
Jennifer: It's next to mine. I'm just telling you where it is. For directions.
-> I'll be there.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: ...Good. I'll have them clean the sand out of the elevator.
-> And if I miss?
    Jennifer: Then I never liked you. Which will be easy, because I don't. #scolding
    Jennifer: Don't miss.
<<elseif $workers > $corporate>>
The girls throw a little party at the stall. Burnt croissants, mostly. Red Velvet finds you at the edge of the lights.
Red Velvet: Tomorrow corporate decides what happens to us. To all of this.
Red Velvet: Whatever they say...erm...I'm glad it was you. Out here. With us.
Red Velvet: With me. I mean, with us! Me is part of us. #cringe
-> I'm glad it was you too.
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: ...Yeah?
    She leans her head on your shoulder. Honey makes a noise and Mocha elbows her.
-> Get some sleep, Red Velvet.
    Red Velvet: You too, boss. Big day.
<<endif>>
===
